"Race guide",
"Ten ways to win, from the undercut to the first car on slicks. Read it any time.",
"How to play",
"Your two AI drivers do the driving. You make the calls from the pit wall.",
"Tyres.",
"Softs are fastest but wear out quickest. Mediums and Hards last longer. In a dry race you must use two different dry compounds.",
"Rain.",
"Pit stop.",
"Tap a tyre under",
"ERS (battery).",
"Deploy for speed on the straights, Harvest to recharge.",
"Battle.",
"Attack to go for gaps, Defend to hold position. Both cost a little.",
"Autonomous.",
"Flip the switch and your AI makes every call. Races you run fully autonomous are marked that way.",
"Boost.",
"The green BOOST button on the race view fires the battery for 12 seconds. Use it when you're within a second of the car ahead.",
"Cameras.",
"Tap any car to follow it. Live (the TV director), Overview, Chase, Cockpit, TV and Pit views. Keys 1–6 on a keyboard, space to pause.",
"Watch the top bar. Once the rain has stopped and it reads Dry, box for slicks that lap. The first car on slicks usually wins.",
"Car 1:",
"Car 2:",
"Tyre wear is high here, so you may need two stops. Box when tyre life drops under 25%.",
"Rain is possible. If a shower is due within two laps of your stop, wait and fit Inters instead. Splitting your two cars covers both bets.",
"If the safety car comes out near your pit window, box straight away: the stop costs about half the time.",
"From the Racing Academy: the fastest car doesn't always win. The best calls do.",
"Pick a plan before the start.",
"Use the engineer's plan, then adjust as the race unfolds. Mediums to start is the safe one-stop. Softs gain places early but wear out fast.",
"Split your two cars.",
"Put them on different tyres or stop on different laps. If the weather or a safety car goes against one, the other benefits.",
"The undercut.",
"Stuck behind someone? Box a lap before they do. Fresh tyres are about a second a lap faster, so you can come out ahead when they stop.",
"Watch tyre life.",
"Under 25%, grip falls off a cliff. Near 0% a tyre can puncture, and a puncture can end your race.",
"Safety car means a cheap stop.",
"A normal stop costs about 8 seconds (a quarter of a lap). Under the safety car it costs about half. If your stop was due in the next few laps, box now.",
"Damp track: Inters. Soaked: Wets. When it dries, the first car on slicks gains the most. The radar in the top bar warns you a few laps ahead.",
"Harvest when you're alone so you have charge for a fight. Then hit BOOST or Deploy when you're within a second of the car ahead, or to defend.",
"Pace.",
"Save tyres on a long stint and Push in the last two laps. Attack makes passes more likely but risks contact. Defend makes you harder to pass.",
"Two compounds.",
"In a dry race you must use two different dry tyres, or you get a 20-second penalty.",
"Pit-exit fights.",
"Coming out just ahead of a rival? Defend and BOOST for the first lap while your new tyres warm up.",
"You call pit stops, tyres and tactics. Your engineer advises.",
"Your AI makes every call. Sit back and watch. You can take over any time.",
"Simple cars",
"Plain blocky cars from the first version. Pick these only if the race stutters on your phone.",
"Intermediate. For a damp track or light rain. Too slow once it dries.",
"Full wet. For heavy rain and standing water.",
"Speed on a dry track",
"In a dry race each car must use two different dry tyres (Soft, Medium or Hard), so every car stops at least once.",
